Item 4 proof sketch: independent exponential clocks; A's m-th sale time = sum Exp(q k), k=1..m = max of m iid Exp(q), cdf (1-e^{-qt})^m; B's = max of m iid Exp(1), density m(1-e^{-t})^{m-1}e^{-t}; after 2m-1 sales A leads iff T_A(m)<T_B(m); u=e^{-t} gives m*int_0^1 (1-u^q)^m (1-u)^{m-1} du. TRUE (and agrees with DP to 1e-16).
Item 5: least N ~ 9.8208e9 (root m = 4,910,424,222.1, N=2m-1 ~ 9,820,848,443; parity offset about half a step, so least N is within a few sales of that). Trust: high for 4-5 figures (formula proven, checked vs DP to 1e-9 at N=1e5, two precisions agree to 1e-18); not checked: monotonicity of P in N over the whole range (only spot values).
